  "notes": "glide: Laysan albatross: white head and body, long narrow pale grey wings four and a half metres across, a pale pink hooked bill. A few circle wide over the swell and the strand on wings held out flat and beaten once or twice in half a minute, more like vultures than gulls, and only now and then come down together on the highest ground near, a ridge or a bleached rib, to sit out the fog. Its own model at 50 mm voxels so the 4.5 m wings fit the 96-voxel grid; long wings in an inner and a tip bone each, a hooked pink bill, dark eyes under a grey brow.",
